{"text": "SUPERIOR COURT OF WASHINGTON FOR KING COUNTY\nIn re: MARISOL ECHEVARRÍA-LUND, Petitioner, and TREVOR J. LUND, Respondent.\nNo. 26-2-11847-3 KNT\nDECLARATION OF PETITIONER IN SUPPORT OF PETITION FOR PROTECTION ORDER (RCW 7.105.100)\nDRAFT - prepared with Eastside Legal Aid Clinic, advocate Dawn Okimoto, 6/22/2026. Petitioner's residential address is confidential under GR 22 and must not appear in the filed version.\nI, Marisol Echevarría-Lund, declare as follows:\n1. I am the Petitioner. I am 34 years old. My date of birth is October 5, 1991. Respondent, Trevor J. Lund, is my husband. His date of birth is 2/11/1987. We married in 2018 and separated on May 2, 2026. We have one child together, Paloma, who is six years old and in kindergarten at Little Cedars Montessori.\n2. I am asking for protection for myself and for Paloma. Since May 2 I have been staying with my sister, Ines Echevarría, in Kent. Before that we lived together at 23418 114th Place SE, Renton, WA 98031. Trevor still lives there.\n3. Most recent incident. On the night of Friday, June 12, 2026, Trevor came to Ines's apartment at about 11:15 p.m. He pounded on the door and yelled that he would \"burn the place down\" if I did not bring Paloma out. He was driving his gray pickup, Washington plate C81 447K. Ines's neighbor, Reggie Tate, saw him and called 911. Kent Police responded (incident no. 26-0041877) but Trevor had left.\n4. Text messages. Between June 12 and June 19, 2026 Trevor sent me 141 text messages from his number, (425) 555-0155, and from a second number I did not recognize, 206.555.0108. Screenshots are attached as Exhibit A. They include: \"you cant hide at ines place forever,\" \"I know what time you get off,\" and a photo of the front door of my work.\n5. Physical violence. On April 18, 2026, during an argument about money, Trevor grabbed my left arm and twisted it behind my back. I was treated the next morning at Harborview Urgent Care - Renton for a fractured left wrist (visit no. UC-3391047). I told the provider I had fallen. That was not true. I was afraid of what he would do if he was arrested. Records are attached as Exhibit B. I was eleven weeks pregnant at the time; I miscarried on April 30.\n6. Firearms. Trevor owns at least two firearms: a 9mm handgun, serial number BFKR447, which he keeps in the truck console, and a hunting rifle. In March he placed the handgun on the kitchen table during an argument and said, \"This is how it ends.\"\n7. Substance use and history. Trevor has used methamphetamine on and off since 2023. He has a 2021 conviction for assault in the fourth degree involving a former girlfriend in Pierce County. He lost his job as a longshoreman in January and blames me.\n8. Surveillance. On June 15 I found a tracking device taped under the rear bumper of my car, a blue 2015 hatchback, plate BXT9920. The device ID printed on it is TG-88-41C7-0093. Trevor also knows the passcode to my phone (0513, Paloma's birthday) and my email password. I have since changed both.\n9. My work. I am a dental hygienist at Cascade Family Dental, 410 Rainier Avenue South, Suite B, Renton. Trevor has come to the parking lot twice since we separated. I ask that he be ordered to stay 1,000 feet away from my work, from Ines's home, and from Paloma's school.\n10. Immigration. Trevor has told me many times that he will \"call immigration\" on me and on my mother. I am a lawful permanent resident; my card number is A-204-417-883. My mother has a pending asylum case. I am afraid for her.\n11. I can be reached through my advocate, Ms. Okimoto, at 206-555-0170 ext. 12 or dokimoto@eastsidelegalaid.example. Please do not send mail to the Renton house.\nI declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of Washington (RCW 9A.72.085) that the foregoing is true and correct.\nSigned at Kent, Washington on ____________, 2026.\n______________________________\nMarisol Echevarría-Lund, Petitioner", "kind": "Rich Text document", "detail": "679 wo